      "20:00  \n\nGood. I’ll give you **3 exact tuning models** depending on your rice condition.  \nNo guessing. Just adjust based on what you have.\n\n---\n\n# 🍚 1️⃣ If Rice is **Freshly Cooked (Hot Now)**\n\n⚠️ Most sensitive stage.\n\n### What to do:\n- Spread rice on wide plate.\n- Add **½ tsp oil or ghee**.\n- Let cool **15–20 mins minimum**.\n- Do NOT add lemon to hot rice.\n\n### Lemon quantity:\n➡️ Use **1.5 tbsp only first**  \nAfter mixing, taste. Add remaining ½ tbsp if needed.\n\nWhy?\nHot rice absorbs acid aggressively → can become sharp later.\n\nBest side:\nPapad or mild potato fry.\n\n---\n\n# ❄️ 2️⃣ If Rice is **Leftover Fridge Rice**\n\nimage_group{\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"separated refrigerated cooked rice grains\",\"breaking clumped rice with fingers\",\"leftover rice in stainless steel bowl\",\"fluffing cold rice before mixing\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\n\nThis is actually **ideal for lemon rice**.\n\n### What to do:\n- Break lumps gently with fingers.\n- Sprinkle 1 tsp warm water.\n- Rest 5 minutes.\n- Then mix tempering.\n\n### Lemon quantity:\n➡️ Full **2 tbsp** works well.\n\nWhy?\nCold rice surface is dry → absorbs flavor evenly.\n\nBest side:\nCurd + pickle (excellent balance).\n\n---\n\n# 🌾 3️⃣ If Rice is Slightly Sticky / Overcooked\n\nDo this correction:\n\n- Add 1 tbsp roasted peanuts extra.\n- Increase tempering oil slightly.\n- Add 1 tsp sesame oil at end.\n\nThis prevents mash texture.\n\n---\n\n# 🥔 Serving Logic (Energy Stability View)\n\n| Side | Effect |\n|------|--------|\n| Curd | Cooling + probiotic |\n| Potato fry | Carb + carb → heavier |\n| Papad | Light crunch, minimal load |\n| Peanut podi | Protein boost |\n\nIf night time → prefer **curd combo**.  \nIf travel / pack → no curd.\n\n---\n\nTell me which category your rice fits.\n\nI’ll lock the exact final ratio like a master recipe."
     ]
    },
