      "15/02/2026 19:52  \n\n## 🍋 Lemon Rice (Elumichai Sadam) – Balanced, Non-Sticky Version\n\nimage_group{\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"South Indian lemon rice in banana leaf\",\"elumichai sadam close up with peanuts\",\"tempered lemon rice with curry leaves and mustard seeds\",\"Tamil style lemon rice with turmeric and roasted peanuts\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\n\nSince you usually prefer **clean structure + exact ratios**, here is a precise version.\n\n---\n\n## 🧂 Ingredients (2 servings)\n\n- Cooked rice – **2 cups** (cooled, grains separate)\n- Lemon juice – **2 tbsp** (fresh)\n- Turmeric powder – **¼ tsp**\n- Salt – **¾ tsp** (adjust)\n- Ghee or oil – **2 tbsp**\n\n### Tempering\n- Mustard seeds – **½ tsp**\n- Urad dal – **1 tsp**\n- Channa dal – **1 tsp**\n- Peanuts – **2 tbsp**\n- Green chilli – **1–2 slit**\n- Dry red chilli – **1**\n- Curry leaves – **1 sprig**\n- Hing (asafoetida) – **1 pinch**\n\nOptional:\n- Ginger finely chopped – **½ tsp**\n- Cashew – 6 pieces\n\n---\n\n## 🔥 Step-by-Step Method\n\n### 1️⃣ Rice Prep (Most Important)\n- Rice must be **completely cooled**.\n- Spread on plate.\n- Add **¼ tsp turmeric + little salt** and gently mix.\n  \n👉 This prevents yellow patches later.\n\n---\n\n### 2️⃣ Tempering (Flavor Core)\nHeat ghee.\n\nAdd in order:\n1. Mustard (let crackle)\n2. Urad + channa dal (light golden)\n3. Peanuts (roast well)\n4. Green chilli + red chilli\n5. Curry leaves\n6. Hing\n7. Ginger (optional)\n\nTurn OFF flame.\n\n---\n\n### 3️⃣ Lemon Activation\nLet tempering cool for **30–40 seconds** (important).\nNow add lemon juice.\n\n👉 If added on high heat → lemon becomes slightly bitter.\n\n---\n\n### 4️⃣ Combine\nPour tempering over rice.\nMix gently (do not mash).\n\nRest 10 minutes before serving.\n\n---\n\n## 🌿 Why Lemon Rice Tastes Better After 30 Minutes?\n\nAcid (lemon) slowly penetrates starch surface.\nOil layer coats grains.\nTurmeric stabilizes colour + mild antimicrobial action.\n\nIt becomes more unified — not sharp, not raw.\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Digestive Logic (You like this part)\n\n- Lemon → increases salivary enzymes.\n- Turmeric → anti-inflammatory.\n- Tempered fats → slow glucose spike.\n- Peanuts → add protein + reduce glycemic load.\n\nCompared to plain rice:\nMore stable energy release.\n\n---\n\n## 🔁 Variations\n\n### 🟢 Temple Style (No onion, no garlic)\nJust follow above base.\n\n### 🟠 Festival Version\nAdd:\n- Cashew\n- More peanuts\n- Little grated coconut (1 tbsp)\n\n### 🔵 Light Morning Version\nReduce ghee to 1 tbsp.\nSkip channa dal.\nAdd grated carrot.\n\n---\n\nIf you tell me:\n- Is rice fresh cooked now?\n- Raw rice or leftover fridge rice?\n- Serving with curd / potato fry / papad?\n\nI will tune ratio exactly to your vessel like we did for samiya upma."
     ]
