     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "20:37  \n\nGood move. 🍋  \nNow we convert **Lemon Rice logic → Lemon Roasted Semiya (Vermicelli)**  \nSame flavor profile. Different starch behavior.\n\n---\n\n## 🍋 Lemon Roasted Semiya Upma (Rice-style Tempering)\n\nimage_group{\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"lemon vermicelli upma South Indian style\",\"roasted semiya lemon upma close up\",\"vermicelli upma with peanuts and curry leaves\",\"Tamil style lemon semiya with turmeric\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\n\n---\n\n## 🧂 Exact Ratios (2 servings)\n\n- Roasted semiya – **1 cup**\n- Water – **1¾ cups**\n- Lemon juice – **1½ tbsp**\n- Turmeric – **¼ tsp**\n- Salt – **¾ tsp**\n- Ghee or oil – **2 tbsp**\n\n### Tempering\n- Mustard – ½ tsp  \n- Urad dal – 1 tsp  \n- Channa dal – 1 tsp  \n- Peanuts – 2 tbsp  \n- Green chilli – 1–2  \n- Red chilli – 1  \n- Curry leaves – 1 sprig  \n- Hing – pinch  \n\nOptional:\n- Ginger – ½ tsp  \n- Cashew – few  \n\n---\n\n# 🔥 Method (Important Difference from Rice)\n\n### 1️⃣ Temper First\nDo full tempering in ghee.\n\n### 2️⃣ Add Water Directly to Tempering\nPour **1¾ cups water** into same pan.\nAdd salt + turmeric.\nBring to boil.\n\n### 3️⃣ Add Semiya\nLower flame.\nAdd roasted semiya gradually.\nStir gently.\n\nCover and cook **4–5 minutes**.\n\nTurn OFF when just cooked (not mushy).\n\n---\n\n### 4️⃣ Lemon Stage (Critical)\nLet it rest **2 minutes**.\nThen add lemon juice.\nMix gently.\n\n👉 Never add lemon while boiling — semiya becomes slightly sticky + dull.\n\n---\n\n# 🧠 Rice vs Semiya – Structural Difference\n\n| Factor | Rice | Semiya |\n|--------|------|--------|\n| Starch density | High | Medium |\n| Absorption speed | Slow | Fast |\n| Overcook risk | Low | High |\n| Lemon penetration | Surface | Full strand |\n\nSemiya absorbs faster → so slightly **less lemon than rice**.\n\n---\n\n# 🌿 Texture Control Tips\n\nIf dry → sprinkle 1 tsp hot water + cover 2 min.  \nIf sticky → add 1 tsp sesame oil + fluff with fork.  \nIf sharp → add 1 tsp ghee to mellow acidity.\n\n---\n\n# 🥗 Serving Pair Logic\n\nNight → Curd best.  \nMorning → Peanut-heavy version.  \nFestival → Add cashew + more tempering.  \nLight version → Skip channa dal.\n\n---\n\nIf you tell:\n- Is your semiya already roasted factory type?\n- Cooker or kadai?\n- Want lemon rice exact taste copy or lighter version?\n\nI’ll tune it exactly like we did earlier."
     ]
