      "20:40  \n\nPerfect.  \n**Roasted packed semiya + Kadai + Exact lemon rice taste**  \nWe will lock it precisely. No softness, no stickiness.\n\n---\n\n# 🍋 Lemon “Rice-Style” Roasted Semiya (Exact Taste Copy)\n\nimage_group{\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"lemon semiya upma South Indian style close up\",\"roasted vermicelli lemon upma with peanuts\",\"Tamil style lemon vermicelli with turmeric and curry leaves\",\"vermicelli upma fluffy separate strands\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\n\n---\n\n## 🧂 Exact Measurements (2 solid servings)\n\n- Roasted semiya – **1 cup (100–110 g)**\n- Water – **1½ cups + 2 tbsp** (very important exact)\n- Lemon juice – **1¾ tbsp**\n- Turmeric – **¼ tsp**\n- Salt – **¾ tsp**\n- Ghee – **1 tbsp**\n- Oil – **1 tbsp**\n\n👉 Mixed fat gives rice-like flavor depth.\n\n---\n\n## 🌶 Tempering (Do Not Skip Anything)\n\n- Mustard – ½ tsp  \n- Urad dal – 1 tsp  \n- Channa dal – 1 tsp  \n- Peanuts – 2 tbsp  \n- Green chilli – 2 slit  \n- Red chilli – 1  \n- Curry leaves – 1 sprig  \n- Hing – pinch  \n- Ginger – ½ tsp finely chopped  \n\nThis tempering is what gives **lemon rice identity**.\n\n---\n\n# 🔥 Kadai Method (Precision Mode)\n\n### 1️⃣ Temper\nHeat ghee + oil.\nAdd mustard → crackle.\nAdd dals → light golden.\nAdd peanuts → roast properly.\nAdd chilli + curry leaves + hing + ginger.\n\n---\n\n### 2️⃣ Add Water\nPour **1½ cups + 2 tbsp water**.\nAdd salt + turmeric.\nBring to rolling boil.\n\n---\n\n### 3️⃣ Add Semiya\nFlame LOW.\nAdd semiya gradually.\nStir once.\nCover lid.\n\nCook **4 minutes only**.\n\nOpen and check:\nWater should be absorbed.\nTexture soft but not mushy.\n\nTurn OFF.\n\n---\n\n### 4️⃣ Lemon Stage (Critical)\nWait 2–3 minutes.\nNow add **1¾ tbsp lemon juice**.\nMix gently with fork.\n\nRest 5–7 minutes before serving.\n\n---\n\n# 🧠 Why Water Reduced Compared to Normal Upma?\n\nNormal upma → 1:2 ratio  \nFor lemon style → slightly drier texture needed  \nSo 1:1.6 approx gives rice-like separation.\n\n---\n\n# 🥜 For 100% Lemon Rice Illusion\n\nAdd at end:\n- 1 tsp sesame oil drizzle  \n- Few crushed roasted peanuts  \n\nNow it tastes extremely close to elumichai sadam.\n\n---\n\nIf texture goes wrong:\n- Sticky → too much water  \n- Dry → sprinkle 1 tbsp hot water + cover  \n- Too sour → add ½ tsp ghee  \n\n---\n\nYou want:\n🔹 Light morning version  \n🔹 Festival heavy version  \n🔹 High-protein version  \n🔹 Kids mild version  \n\nTell me. I’ll adjust precisely."
     ]
