     "parts": [
      "16/02/2025 19:28  \n\nYes — you *can* add pepper powder.  \nBut timing and quantity matter.\n\n---\n\n## 🌶 Should You Add Pepper in Lemon Semiya?\n\n### ✅ If you want:\n- Slight heat\n- Deeper temple-style flavour\n- Better digestion (especially night)\n\nThen add **very little**.\n\n---\n\n## 🧂 Exact Quantity (for 1 cup semiya)\n\n➡️ **¼ tsp maximum**  \n\nMore than that → it overpowers lemon.\n\n---\n\n## ⏱ When to Add?\n\nTwo safe options:\n\n### Option 1 (Balanced – Recommended)\nAdd pepper powder into boiling water stage  \n(along with salt + turmeric)\n\nThis mellows it.\n\n---\n\n### Option 2 (Stronger heat)\nAdd pepper at final mixing stage  \n(after lemon)\n\nThis gives sharper spice.\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Flavor Logic\n\nLemon = bright, acidic  \nPepper = warm, deep heat  \n\nTogether → slightly closer to mild **pepper rasam profile** but dry version.\n\nIf you already added:\n- Green chilli  \n- Red chilli  \n\nThen keep pepper very low.\n\n---\n\n## My Suggestion (Exact Taste Mode)\n\nAdd:\n- ⅛ tsp pepper powder only  \n- Or lightly crush 4–5 whole peppercorns instead\n\nThat keeps lemon dominant.\n\n---\n\nIf this is night dinner, pepper is good.  \nIf morning tiffin, skip or keep very mild.\n\nTell me — already added chilli how much?"
